FROM (VALUES
  ('b4e91302-a865-44b6-9608-56f45869715f','STRAIGHT N ARROW 3D ARCHERY, based in Belington, West Virginia, holds USA Archery affiliation with 3D Archery listed as its program focus, an interesting combination since 3D-format shooting is more commonly associated with ASA than with USA Archery''s Olympic-style recurve and compound target disciplines. That pairing suggests this club may bridge both worlds, using USA Archery''s structure while running 3D-style rounds for its members. Belington sits in the mountainous heart of West Virginia, terrain that lends itself naturally to a 3D course with varied elevation and cover between target positions. No lane counts, pro shop, or lesson details are listed, so reach out directly to confirm schedules and how to participate.'),
  ('2f6d935b-9c60-48e1-929a-f584f80f42a5','STRAIGHT-N-ARROW ARCHERS operates in Minerva, a small town in eastern Ohio, as a USA Archery affiliated club running both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program and an Adult Archery Program. Offering both tracks in one small-town location gives area families a single place to bring archers of different ages rather than needing separate youth and adult facilities. Eastern Ohio''s mix of rural and small-town communities means a structured, affiliated club like this likely draws members from a fairly wide radius rather than just Minerva itself. Meeting times, costs, and facility details aren''t listed, so contact the club directly to find out current program schedules and how to join.'),
  ('5b68a6f3-52a3-4617-9317-dd303daafc57','Strictly Archery, based in Shorewood, Illinois, combines USA Archery affiliation with a pro shop and lessons alongside both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program and an Adult Archery Program, making it one of the more full-service listings in the Chicago-area suburbs. Having retail, instruction, and structured youth and adult pathways all under one roof means a family could realistically outfit a new archer, get them coached, and enroll them in a JOAD program without leaving the building. Shorewood sits in the fast-growing southwest Chicago suburbs, a market with plenty of demand for beginner-friendly archery options. Class schedules, pricing, and inventory aren''t listed, so contact Strictly Archery directly for current details.'),
  ('8e3be518-41f5-4738-ab41-5b0b970aaeed','StudioX Archery, located in Cupertino, California, in the heart of Silicon Valley, is a USA Archery affiliated club running both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program and an Adult Archery Program. The ''Studio'' framing in the name suggests an indoor, urban-style setup more common in dense Bay Area suburbs than the outdoor ranges found in rural parts of the state, though that''s an inference from the name rather than a confirmed detail. Cupertino''s tech-heavy demographic and limited open space make a structured, indoor-capable club a practical fit for local families wanting archery instruction close to home. Class times, costs, and facility details aren''t listed, so contact StudioX Archery directly for current offerings.'),
  ('f99f28b1-c1b8-4528-8870-f3d2ddf5f5d8','Suffolk Archers, based in Huntington Station on New York''s Long Island, holds USA Archery affiliation with a Junior Olympic Archery Development program, and also runs both a 3D course and a field archery course, giving members access to marked-distance field rounds and varied 3D shooting alongside structured youth instruction. That range of formats is fairly comprehensive for a Long Island club, an area where open land for archery courses is more limited than in rural upstate settings. Suffolk County has a steady base of archery and bowhunting participants, and a club offering this much variety likely draws members from across the county. Contact the club directly for JOAD enrollment and course access details.'),
  ('b55c1b48-8528-4f32-bba2-695d1145ea9d','Summit Archery sits in Heber City, Utah, a mountain valley community between Park City and Provo, and holds USA Archery affiliation with both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program and an Adult Archery Program on offer. Heber City''s setting among the Wasatch mountains puts it within easy reach of both Park City''s recreation-focused crowd and the more rural Heber Valley community, giving a structured archery club here a fairly broad potential membership base. Running JOAD and adult programs together allows one club to serve multiple generations of the same family, a practical setup for a smaller mountain town. Schedules, costs, and enrollment details aren''t listed, so reach out to Summit Archery directly for current information.'),
  ('f5e259fd-40fe-489f-887d-ef7658f03ab0','Suncoast Archers operates in Parrish, Florida, a fast-growing community between Tampa and Sarasota, as a volunteer club with an ASA 3D archery affiliation. Scott Tussing is listed as the contact, the person to reach about shoot dates, course conditions, and how membership works, since the club doesn''t appear to publish a detailed public schedule. Florida''s Gulf Coast has an active bowhunting and 3D archery following, and a club situated between two growing metro areas likely draws members from a fairly wide surrounding radius. There''s no listed detail on lane counts or amenities beyond the ASA affiliation itself, so Scott Tussing remains the best channel for information on getting involved or attending a shoot.'),
  ('891e5ba6-d717-45cd-82f1-b115985ee098','SW ARCHERY ACADEMY in Paramus, New Jersey runs an unusually wide set of USA Archery affiliated programs for one club: Junior Olympic Archery Development, an Adult Archery Program, 3D Archery, and Field Archery. Covering four distinct pathways under one academy name suggests a facility built to handle everything from a first-time youth archer to an adult looking for field-style marked-distance rounds or 3D practice, a broad offering that''s uncommon in the densely built-out New York suburbs of Bergen County. Paramus is a major retail and residential hub just outside New York City, and an academy with this much program depth is well positioned to serve a large, varied population. Enrollment details, schedules, and costs aren''t listed, so contact SW Archery Academy directly.'),
  ('a88e9d90-db1c-42a6-b9e5-d96ad7f62cf6','Swamp Fox Archery and Bow Club, in Tabor City near North Carolina''s border with South Carolina, is a volunteer club with an ASA 3D archery affiliation. The ''Swamp Fox'' name echoes Francis Marion, the Revolutionary War guerrilla fighter nicknamed the Swamp Fox for his exploits in this same coastal Carolina region, a nod to local history rather than the club''s programming. Jamie Sumner is listed as the contact for questions on shoot schedules or joining, since the club''s regular operations aren''t detailed publicly here. Southeastern North Carolina''s mix of swamp and pine woodland is well suited to a 3D course, and clubs like this typically serve local bowhunters ahead of the fall season. Reach out to Jamie Sumner for current information.'),
  ('28353097-1a6c-4dc7-9361-93fa6d371c76','Sweetwater Archery Club is based in Winston, Georgia, a small community west of Atlanta, and runs as a volunteer club with an ASA 3D archery affiliation. Kevin Hawk is listed as the contact, the right person to reach about shoot dates or how to join, since the club doesn''t appear to publish a detailed schedule elsewhere. West Georgia''s rolling, wooded terrain outside metro Atlanta suits a 3D-style course well, and a club here likely serves both dedicated 3D competitors and local bowhunters using the course to prepare for deer season. No lane counts or additional facility details are listed, so Kevin Hawk or the club directly remains the best source for confirming details before visiting.'),
  ('c3bc8e83-0ac4-41d2-929b-61a7d727155f','Swift River Sportsman''s Club in Belchertown, Massachusetts runs as a volunteer club plugged into the ASA 3D archery circuit, the kind of setup where members take turns keeping the range and course in shape rather than paying staff to do it. Western Massachusetts has a steady bowhunting population, and a club affiliated with ASA generally means realistic animal targets and a scoring format built around bowhunting practice rather than pure target rounds. Dana Charbonneau is listed as a contact, a solid first stop for anyone curious about shoot dates or how to join. Beyond the 3D affiliation, specifics on hours or facilities aren''t posted, so calling or reaching out to Dana ahead of a visit is the practical move.'),
  ('3e830efe-7196-4973-929c-7f7e7dbec5d7','Sylvan Archers Inc, based in Sherwood, Oregon just outside Portland, is a USA Archery affiliated club running both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program and an Adult Archery Program, plus a 3D course and a field course on site. That combination, JOAD for young shooters, an adult track, and two different course formats, points to a genuinely full-service club rather than a single-discipline group, which is a rarer find in the Pacific Northwest archery scene. Families looking for structured youth coaching alongside adults wanting their own progression path both have a real entry point here. Specific schedules and fees for each program aren''t listed, so reaching out directly is the way to sort out which track fits.'),
  ('b463488a-05be-4b24-9c86-9dc5c9fcdbf8','Synergy Archery Alliance operates out of Woodlawn, Tennessee, just north of Clarksville, as a volunteer-run club with ASA affiliation putting it in the 3D archery and bowhunting-practice camp. Middle Tennessee has a dense concentration of these member-run clubs, and the ASA tie generally means a scored course of foam animal targets rather than paper bullseyes, appealing most to hunters keeping their form sharp between seasons. Arthur Clark is the listed contact, worth reaching out to for shoot schedules or membership steps since the club doesn''t appear to post that information elsewhere. As with most volunteer operations, showing up unannounced is a gamble, so a call or message ahead of time is the better plan.'),
  ('f86398e1-595a-460e-84f5-4970dc693e8f','T-Town Drillers JOAD in Tulsa, Oklahoma runs a full slate under USA Archery affiliation: Junior Olympic Archery Development for young shooters, an Adult Archery Program, plus both 3D and field archery formats. That breadth, four distinct offerings under one club, suggests a program built to keep archers engaged as they grow rather than one narrowly focused on a single age group or style. Tulsa''s archery scene benefits from having a club willing to run youth development alongside adult and outdoor-format shooting in the same organization. Actual meeting times, costs, and which programs are currently active aren''t detailed here, so contacting the club directly is the right next step for anyone wanting to join a session.'),
  ('16c15e66-283f-445b-85f4-be53cc455aef','Talladega County Bowhunters, based in Lincoln, Alabama, is a volunteer club with ASA affiliation, tying it into the competitive 3D archery world that many Southern bowhunters use to stay sharp through the off-season. The name itself signals a hunting-first identity rather than a target-archery club, which tracks with the ASA connection and the strong bowhunting culture found across east-central Alabama. Wes Patterson is listed as the contact, a good starting point for anyone wanting to know about shoot dates, dues, or how the club''s course is laid out, since none of that is posted publicly. As with most member-run clubs, a message to Wes ahead of a visit beats showing up cold.'),
  ('6a678042-2eea-4fd1-a37a-8fb4194151f4','Tallahassee Archery Club in Florida''s capital is a volunteer club with ASA affiliation that stands out for running a genuinely full program: a 3D course, a field course, and lessons all under one roof. That''s an unusually complete offering for a member-run club, covering hunters who want realistic animal targets, archers who prefer the varied-distance field format, and total beginners who need instruction to get started. North Florida''s bowhunting community has a solid anchor point in a club willing to teach as well as compete. Richard Mann is the listed contact for anyone wanting specifics on scheduling or joining, since day-to-day details like dues and course hours aren''t published beyond that.'),
  ('c24c2f6d-6903-4ebd-8bde-ecc321a44c12','Tampa Archers, located in Land O'' Lakes, Florida just north of Tampa, is a USA Archery affiliated club running both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program and an Adult Archery Program, on top of a 3D course and lessons. That''s a wide spread of offerings, youth Olympic-style development, an adult track, bowhunting-style 3D targets, and instruction, giving the club appeal across very different kinds of archers in the greater Tampa Bay area. A family with kids in JOAD and a parent wanting their own lessons could realistically both find a home here. Program costs, schedules, and which sessions are currently running aren''t detailed, so a direct inquiry is the way to sort out specifics.'),
  ('e6afdfba-3754-4866-920e-a4a4ddd6e552','Tampa Bay Sporting Clays and Archery, also in Land O'' Lakes, Florida, pairs its archery side with sporting clays under one roof, and the archery portion runs as a volunteer club with ASA affiliation and its own 3D course. That combined format is a bit unusual, a facility serving both shotgun and bow sports gives it a broader draw than a single-discipline club, and the ASA tie means the 3D course is built around the realistic-target, bowhunting-practice style rather than pure target rounds. Edwin Griffin is listed as the archery contact for anyone wanting details on the course or how to get involved. Hours and access specifics for the archery side aren''t posted, so reaching out to Edwin directly is the move.'),
  ('5039d0c3-f8bc-45a5-af9a-130f15ec7eda','Team SPIDERx, located in Spring, Texas just north of Houston, is a USA Archery affiliated club running both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program and an Adult Archery Program. Having both tracks under one club gives the greater Houston area a spot where a family can bring kids into JOAD''s Olympic-style coaching while a parent works through the adult program in parallel, rather than needing two separate organizations. The Houston metro has a competitive archery culture, and a club with structured youth and adult pathways is well positioned within it. Meeting schedules, costs, and current enrollment status for each program aren''t posted here, so reaching out directly is the way to get specifics before signing up.'),
  ('ba9e8788-d5c4-4187-b5a3-fbdd9947cc3d','Team Triangle Archery serves Chapel Hill, North Carolina as a USA Archery affiliated club running a Junior Olympic Archery Development program, putting the focus squarely on youth Olympic-style coaching in the Research Triangle area. That region has a strong base of academic and youth-sports families, and a JOAD program gives parents a structured, nationally recognized pathway for kids interested in target archery rather than an informal drop-in setup. No detail is listed here on adult programs, course type, or facility specifics, so the club''s public information centers on its JOAD offering. Anyone wanting to enroll a young archer or learn more about schedules and cost should contact the club directly.'),
  ('ca86cba0-ee6d-4476-a39d-7f050544fcb5','Tejas JOAD Archery in Frisco, Texas runs a genuinely broad program under USA Archery affiliation: Junior Olympic Archery Development, an Adult Archery Program, 3D archery, field archery, and lessons all in one club. That''s about as complete a lineup as a single archery club can offer, covering Olympic-style youth coaching, adult participation, two different outdoor course formats, and direct instruction for newcomers. Frisco sits in the fast-growing north Dallas suburbs, an area with plenty of families looking for structured youth activities, and a club this comprehensive is well suited to that demand. Specific schedules and costs for each program aren''t listed, so a direct inquiry is the way to sort out which track to start with.'),
  ('bc59183f-bf3d-446b-b01c-e52863406214','Tennessee Archery in Memphis is a USA Archery affiliated club offering a Junior Olympic Archery Development program, an Adult Archery Program, and lessons, giving West Tennessee a structured option for archers of any age or experience level. Memphis is a large metro without an overwhelming number of dedicated archery clubs, so one running both youth Olympic-style development and adult instruction under a single organization is a meaningful resource for local families and newcomers alike. The lesson component in particular lowers the barrier for someone who''s never picked up a bow before. Program schedules, fees, and current enrollment aren''t listed here, so reaching out to the club directly is the way to get real answers.'),
  ('0ba7d712-1898-4e03-a1ab-688e2e54e12d','Texas Elite 3-D Archery, based in Columbus, Texas between Houston and San Antonio, is a club with a past ASA affiliation, though the listed status notes that affiliation expired in 2025. That detail matters for anyone assuming an active ASA connection today, since it suggests the club''s competitive 3D ties may have lapsed or be in the process of renewing rather than currently active. Columbus sits along a rural stretch of I-10 with a solid hunting base, the kind of area where a 3D-format club naturally fits the local bowhunting calendar. Given the uncertain affiliation status, anyone interested should contact the club directly to confirm what''s currently running before assuming ASA-sanctioned shoots are still on the calendar.'),
