  ('899a2aa5-1a47-4b7d-81d2-ccae11769bf4','The Archery and Bow Club, located in Gray Court, South Carolina, is a volunteer club with ASA affiliation and its own 3D course, placing it within the bowhunting-practice tradition common across the South Carolina upstate. Gray Court is a small community between Greenville and Laurens, and a club like this often serves as the primary organized archery outlet for archers scattered across that rural stretch. The ASA tie and 3D course together point to a group built around scored, realistic-target shooting that doubles as hunting-season tune-up practice. Al Brandon is listed as the contact for anyone wanting to know about shoot schedules or how to join, since further details aren''t posted publicly.'),
  ('7c29dc6e-69b6-495b-86be-50ab57e8ac45','The City of Yuma runs a USA Archery-affiliated program that combines a Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) pathway for young shooters with a separate Adult Archery Program, making it a rare municipally-tied option in this part of Arizona for archers of any age to get structured instruction. Being a hybrid facility rather than a pure club or commercial range suggests it likely draws on city recreation resources alongside a more traditional club structure. Yuma''s desert climate supports outdoor archery much of the year, and a JOAD pipeline in the area gives local kids an actual path from beginner lessons toward competitive shooting. Contacting the program directly is the way to confirm current session schedules.'),
  ('61cb3243-cdf8-44cb-bbb1-4841ccd5c1df','The Club House in Gaston, Indiana operates as a commercial archery business and carries an IBO-listed pro shop, meaning it''s recognized within the International Bowhunting Organization''s own directory as a resource for gear and service. That IBO tie suggests a shop oriented toward serious bowhunters and 3D competitors rather than casual walk-ins only, which fits Indiana''s strong bowhunting culture. Small-town Gaston sits within reach of several rural Indiana counties where a pro shop like this can be one of the closer options for bow work, arrow setup, or general archery supplies. No other amenities or program details are listed, so confirming hours and services directly is worthwhile before a visit.'),
