  ('f73b0254-8d74-4be0-82bf-a7075f5a125e','The Mountain Archery in San Leandro runs as a USA Archery-affiliated hybrid facility, meaning it combines structured national-governing-body programs with more of a club feel on the ground. Its lineup includes a Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) track for younger shooters and a separate Adult Archery Program, giving both kids and grown-ups an actual instructional pathway rather than just open range time. The East Bay''s dense population supports demand for programs like this, and being USA Archery-affiliated typically means coaching follows recognized national standards. No lane counts or additional amenities are listed publicly, so anyone interested in enrolling in JOAD or the adult program should reach out directly for current schedules.'),
  ('074ace66-062c-4c6f-b391-6f634730c3fa','The Other Place Archery Club in Kingstree, South Carolina runs as a volunteer-organized, ASA-affiliated 3D archery club, tying it into the Archery Shooters Association''s realistic-target competition format rather than pure target archery. That 3D focus tends to draw a bowhunting-minded membership in this part of the Lowcountry, where hunting is a significant part of local culture. Robert Mc Clary is listed as a contact for the club, which is the practical way in for anyone wanting to know about course conditions, shoot dates, or how membership works, since the club doesn''t appear to post detailed public information beyond that. Reaching out directly remains the best route before planning a visit.'),
